From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: gate SSPM-dependent ACPI paths on firmware presence

GB10 firmware describes the MT8901 Power Wrap, SPI and DSP devices while
marking the SSPM mailbox absent. The USB4 resource-release hook still
arms, and the SPI and DSP power drivers try to obtain SSPM-backed control.
Each call fails with -ENODEV because the transport cannot be initialized.

Require a firmware-present SSPM device before arming the release hook or
probing these SSPM-only ACPI clients. Leave Power Wrap's other setup and
the SPI device-tree path unchanged. This is not a transport-ready check:
a present mailbox whose driver or firmware fails still takes the existing
error path. Do not claim successful power transitions without a transport.

Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/power_wrap/power_wrap.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/power_wrap/power_wrap.c
@@ -829,6 +829,11 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* Firmware can describe MT8901 while hiding the SSPM mailbox. */
+	if (!acpi_dev_present("MTKW8400", NULL, -1) &&
+	    !acpi_dev_present("NVDA8400", NULL, -1))
+		return;
+
 	mutex_lock(&pwrap_usb4_lock);
 	pwrap_usb4_dev = dev;
 	pwrap_usb4_nb.notifier_call = pwrap_usb4_bus_notify;
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c
@@ -1331,6 +1331,12 @@
 	bool has_of = dev->of_node != NULL;
 	bool has_acpi = has_acpi_companion(dev);
 
+	/* The ACPI path requires SSPM to control clocks and power. */
+	if (!has_of && has_acpi &&
+	    !acpi_dev_present("MTKW8400", NULL, -1) &&
+	    !acpi_dev_present("NVDA8400", NULL, -1))
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	host = devm_spi_alloc_host(dev, sizeof(*mdata));
 	if (!host)
 		return -ENOMEM;
--- a/sound/soc/sof/mediatek/mt8901/mt8901.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sof/mediatek/mt8901/mt8901.c
@@ -51,6 +51,11 @@
 
 	adev = ACPI_COMPANION(dev);
 	if (!adev)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	/* This driver only manages DSP power through the SSPM mailbox. */
+	if (!acpi_dev_present("MTKW8400", NULL, -1) &&
+	    !acpi_dev_present("NVDA8400", NULL, -1))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	priv = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*priv), GFP_KERNEL);
